Consider these two series:

$\begin{align}
\textrm{I}.&\displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\dfrac{(-1)^n}{n^{^{2p}}}
\\\\
\textrm{II}.&\displaystyle\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\dfrac{1}{n^{^{p}}}
\end{align}$

**Pick all of the following values of $p$ for which both series $\textrm{I}$ and series $\textrm{II}$ converge.**

[[☃ radio 1]]
